                    text: "**Motherson Sumi Wiring** bought ₹5,243cr of goods from its promoter groups in FY26 plus ₹216cr from other related parties, about 70% of a ₹7,742cr material bill, pays rent of about ₹99cr and a ₹60.9cr management fee to them, and asked shareholders to approve up to ₹75cr of royalty and ₹922cr of purchases from Sumitomo for FY27; the auditor made arm’s-length pricing a key audit matter. **Lumax** paid Stanley ₹57.8cr of royalty (₹39.3cr a year earlier), bought ₹322cr from Stanley companies and ₹478cr from promoter-group Lumax companies, and paid ₹31.6cr of service charges to another. **Dhoot** pays Bain Capital’s Indian advisers ₹12cr a year and owed a lump sum of about ₹48cr on listing, and bought ₹21.7cr of equipment from promoter-group Mangalam Capital. Smaller flows run at **Minda** (₹27.8cr of rent to a promoter company), **Pricol** (about ₹36cr) and **Divgi** (₹4.5cr of ‘machine and development charges’). **My view: Motherson Sumi Wiring’s dependence is structural and disclosed; minority holders rely entirely on arm’s-length pricing they cannot check.**",
